   "source": [
    "# Correlation heatmap and summary table\n",
    "corr_matrix = train[core_features + [\"TARGET\"]].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "mask = np.triu(np.ones_like(corr_matrix, dtype=bool))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, fmt=\".2f\", cmap=\"vlag\", center=0,\n",
    "            mask=mask, linewidths=0.5, cbar_kws={\"shrink\": 0.8})\n",
    "plt.title(\"Correlation Matrix: PDF Security Features & TARGET\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print top correlations with target\n",
    "top_corr = corr_matrix[\"TARGET\"].drop(\"TARGET\").sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "print(\"Correlation with TARGET (Phishing Risk):\")\n",
    "display(pd.DataFrame({\"Pearson Correlation (r)\": top_corr}))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec3_3\"></a>\n",
    "### 3.3 Summary Findings & Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on the visualization and exploratory data analysis:\n",
    "1. **Zero Missing Data in Features**: Clean dataset with 100% complete feature columns once trailing export artifacts are dropped.\n",
    "2. **High Predictive Separation**: Features like `entropy_of_streams`, `total_filters`, `object_count`, and `valid_pdf_header` display strong correlation and divergence between classes.\n",
    "3. **Heavy Tailing**: Structural counters require standardization (`StandardScaler`) to ensure balanced model convergence.\n",
    "4. **Balanced Classes**: 51.8% vs 48.2% allows fair evaluation without extreme sampling adjustments, reinforced by `class_weight='balanced'`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### **[Next Steps]**\n",
    "- Standardize all 10 features using `StandardScaler` to put them on a uniform scale ($\\mu=0, \\sigma=1$).\n",
    "- Save standardized and raw datasets to CSV in `output/pdf output/`.\n",
    "- Train and evaluate 3 distinct algorithms: **Logistic Regression**, **Decision Tree**, and **Random Forest**.\n",
    "- Implement multimodal majority voting consensus compatible with `InterfaceExplainPhish`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec4\"></a>\n",
    "## 4. Preprocessing and Feature Creation\n",
    "Here, we conduct preprocessing and feature transformation based on what we learned in the visualization stage.\n",
    "\n",
    "We apply log-scaling to heavy-tailed attributes for linear models and compute standardized feature arrays.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.599949Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.598947Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.608979Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.608469Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Engineered log features added. Feature count: 14 attributes.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Preprocessing: compute log-transformed structural features\n",
    "train_proc = train.copy()\n",
    "test_proc = test.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in [\"file_size\", \"text_length\", \"object_count\", \"total_filters\"]:\n",
    "    train_proc[f\"{col}_log\"] = np.log1p(train_proc[col])\n",
    "    test_proc[f\"{col}_log\"] = np.log1p(test_proc[col])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Engineered log features added. Feature count: {train_proc.shape[1] - 2} attributes.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec5\"></a>\n",
    "## 5. Building the Machine Learning Model\n",
    "Now, we are ready to start building the machine learning models.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec5_1\"></a>\n",
    "### 5.1 Import Additional Libraries\n",
    "We import scikit-learn modules for model building, validation, metrics, and visualization:\n",
    "- `StandardScaler` for zero-mean, unit-variance scaling\n",
    "- `LogisticRegression` for parametric linear classification\n",
    "- `DecisionTreeClassifier` for non-linear rule extraction\n",
    "- `RandomForestClassifier` for ensemble bagging\n",
    "- Evaluation metrics: `roc_auc_score`, `accuracy_score`, `confusion_matrix`, `classification_report`\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.610983Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.610983Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.778820Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.778820Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Machine learning libraries imported successfully!"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, plot_tree\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    roc_auc_score, accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n",
    "    f1_score, confusion_matrix, roc_curve\n",
    ")\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Machine learning libraries imported successfully!\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec5_2\"></a>\n",
    "### 5.2 Preparing the Data\n",
    "Split the data into explanatory and target variables. The target variable is `TARGET` and the explanatory variables are the 10 core PDF features matching the **`InterfaceExplainPhish`** extractor schema.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.780920Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.780920Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.787725Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-03T08:15:22.787725Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "X shape: (11577, 10), y shape: (11577,), X_test shape: (7719, 10)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Define the core 10 PDF features matching InterfaceExplainPhish extractor schema\n",
    "use_features = [\n",
    "    \"text_length\",\n",
    "    \"object_count\",\n",
    "    \"file_size\",\n",
    "    \"metadata_size\",\n",
    "    \"title_chars\",\n",
    "    \"total_filters\",\n",
    "    \"entropy_of_streams\",\n",
    "    \"stream_count\",\n",
    "    \"endstream_count\",\n",
    "    \"valid_pdf_header\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Split into explanatory and target variables\n",
    "X = train[use_features].values\n",
    "y = train[\"TARGET\"].values\n",
    "X_test = test[use_features].values\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"X shape: {X.shape}, y shape: {y.shape}, X_test shape: {X_test.shape}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Standardize the data. Standardization transforms values so the mean is 0 and variance is 1 ($z = \\frac{x - \\mu}{\\sigma}$). This ensures fast and stable convergence for Logistic Regression and consistent distance calculations.\n"
   ]
  },
